    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Benoît Jutras, (born 1963) is a Canadian composer. Jutras is best known for his work with the Canadian entertainment company Cirque du Soleil, first as music director and later as composer for several of the company's contemporary circus shows. Jutras' music often blends eclectic influences, including world beat, classical, rock, trip hop, and electronica. His scores for Cirque du Soleil shows include \"O\", \"Mystère\", \"Quidam\", and \"La Nouba\". His work outside of Cirque du Soleil has included original soundtracks for \"Le Rêve\" (a show at the Wynn resort in Las Vegas), the \"Glow in the Park Parade\" (a nighttime parade at Six Flags theme parks), and \"The House of Dancing Water\" (a show at the City of Dreams resort in Macau). He has also composed for film and television.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
